From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:17:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the shaping of layouts alike

LayoutContext keeps what shaping a layout's text gave (ShapeCache). The
next layout reuses it when it has the same text, the same inline box
positions and the same analysis (scripts, breaks, bidi levels), and is
styled the same in what changes shaping: the font stack, size, width,
style, weight, variations, features, locale, letter and word spacing.

Its other styles (colors, line height, line breaking) may differ. Each
character and shaped cluster takes the new layout's style index
(ShapedText::set_style_indices).

A browser shapes the same text again as content is built again, and
alike text in alike elements. The cache holds up to 2^18 characters,
then starts again.

In a debug build every kept shaping is also shaped again and compared,
with fonts compared by their data: a kept shaping holds the copy of a
font file it was made with, and fontique loads a file again once nothing
holds its copy.
